<task id="041" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Membership derivation + reconcile job (open via ADR-034; reconcile ACS from Dataverse; event + sweep)</title>
    <phase>W4 — Thread Resolver + Membership + Privacy</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>040,011</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, jobs</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a background reconcile job + membership-derivation service touching `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Jobs/`, calling ACS membership mutation (Add/RemoveParticipants). Membership-as-projection is a security-relevant invariant (ACS must never exceed Dataverse-derived access); touches `.cs`; FULL protocol + Step 9.5 gates.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-07, NFR-02</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Derive a thread's authorized participant set from Dataverse and reconcile ACS thread membership to match it — ACS membership is a **reconciled PROJECTION of Dataverse-derived access, never a second ACL**.

    • **Open (record-anchored) threads**: membership derives from `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034) — Spaarke's canonical "who is associated with this matter/record" (owner, assigned attorney, assigned firm, …). No record access → no membership.
    • **1:1 direct threads**: membership is the explicit two-participant list (from task 043's model).
    • **Private threads**: add an explicit per-record sharing grant (mechanism decided in task 002) on top of the derived set.

    A **reconcile job** recomputes the authorized set and reconciles ACS thread participants via server-side `ChatThreadClient.AddParticipants` / `RemoveParticipant`, driven **event-driven** (Dataverse record-access change | privacy switch | participant edit) **AND** a **periodic sweep** (eventual consistency safety net). Dataverse is authoritative; ACS is the projection. **Write an audit entry per membership change.** Reuse the existing Service Bus job contract (idempotency, retry, DLQ). Best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02) — a reconcile failure does not fail send/capture; the sweep repairs drift.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem + background-job infrastructure. Authority on `Services/Communication/`, `Services/Jobs/`, ADR-034 (`MembershipResolverService`), ADR-004/ADR-036 (job contract), ADR-028 (central `TokenCredential`; server-side ACS ops), §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. You hold the "membership is a projection, never a second source of truth" invariant as load-bearing.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A membership-derivation path computes a thread's authorized participant set (open → ADR-034 `MembershipResolverService`; 1:1 → explicit two-party list; private → derived set + explicit grant), and a reconcile job (event-driven + periodic sweep, on the existing Service Bus job contract) reconciles ACS thread participants (Add/Remove) to match it, writing an audit entry per change. ACS membership never exceeds Dataverse-derived access. Best-effort/non-fatal. Build clean; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported; Step 9.5 FULL gates run; `/conflict-check` clean before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §4 (membership sync) + §5 (privacy) + §8.4 (ACS membership sync): "Dataverse is authoritative; ACS membership is the projection. Eventually consistent — reconcile via event + periodic sweep." ACS won't deliver *live* messages to a non-member, so ACS keeps its own thread membership; we reconcile it FROM Dataverse access. It is never a second source of truth — the access boundary is always the Dataverse record (design §5).

      **Component Justification (§11) for the reconcile job:**
      1. **Existing** — `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034) already answers "who is associated with this record"; the Service Bus job contract already exists (`Services/Jobs/`). This task adds a thin derivation-to-ACS reconcile job, not a new membership engine (verify by grep before claiming none).
      2. **Extension** — Reuse `IMembershipResolverService` for derivation and the existing job contract for scheduling/retry/DLQ; the net-new piece is the derivation→ACS reconcile step + audit, which has no existing home.
      3. **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete failure)** — Without reconcile, ACS thread membership drifts from Dataverse access: a user removed from a matter still receives live chat (over-exposure), or a newly-added attorney can't participate (under-exposure). That is a named security/functional failure (FR-07, NFR-06 adjacency), not "future flexibility."

      **Invariant to protect:** ACS membership ⊆ Dataverse-derived access, ALWAYS. Reconcile only ADDs members that Dataverse authorizes and REMOVEs members Dataverse no longer authorizes. Never grant ACS membership beyond the derived set.

      **Scope discipline:** derivation + reconcile job + audit. Do NOT build a new authorization engine (reuse ADR-034). Do NOT build a notification fabric (R1 polls). ACS membership mutation is server-side only (no client token).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IThreadResolver.cs (task 040 — thread identity)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Acs/ (task 011 — ACS thread + membership ops: Add/RemoveParticipants)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ (job contract: idempotency, retry, DLQ)</file>
      <file>IMembershipResolverService (ADR-034 — open-thread membership derivation)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/PlaybookSharingService.cs / sprk_externalrecordaccess (private-grant precedent — task 002 decides the detail)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-07">Open (record-anchored) membership derives from `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034); 1:1 direct uses the explicit two-participant list; private threads add an explicit per-record sharing grant. A job reconciles ACS thread participants from Dataverse-derived access (event-driven + periodic sweep). Audit entry per change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-INVARIANT">ACS membership is a reconciled PROJECTION of Dataverse-derived access, NEVER a second ACL. ACS membership MUST NOT exceed the Dataverse-derived authorized set.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Derive open-thread membership via `IMembershipResolverService` — do NOT reimplement association logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004,ADR-036">Reuse the existing Service Bus job contract — idempotency, retry, dead-letter. Reconcile is a background job, not inline in the send/capture path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">ACS membership mutation is server-side only via the central `TokenCredential`/ACS ops from task 011; MUST NOT `new` a credential; no client token.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Best-effort/non-fatal — a reconcile failure MUST NOT fail send or inbound-capture; the periodic sweep repairs drift. Log + retry + DLQ.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register the derivation service + job via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-032 Null-Object if feature-gated; unconditional endpoint/job registration).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

