    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Derived membership (ADR-034)" location="IMembershipResolverService">
        Ask `IMembershipResolverService` "who is associated with this record" for the thread's anchor; that set IS the open-thread membership. Do not recompute association.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Event + sweep reconcile" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/">
        Enqueue a reconcile job on Dataverse access change / privacy switch / participant edit (event-driven), and run a periodic sweep for eventual-consistency safety. Idempotent — reconciling an already-consistent thread is a no-op.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Projection, not ACL" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Acs/">
        Compute desired = Dataverse-derived set; current = ACS participants; Add (desired \ current), Remove (current \ desired). Never add beyond desired.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read task 040's `IThreadResolver` (thread identity + anchor), task 011's ACS membership ops (Add/RemoveParticipants), `IMembershipResolverService` (ADR-034), and the `Services/Jobs/` contract (idempotency/retry/DLQ). Confirm task 002's private-grant decision.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + root §11 + ADR-034 + ADR-004/036 before designing the derivation service + job.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement membership derivation: for a thread, compute the authorized participant set — open (record-anchored) via `IMembershipResolverService` on the thread's ADR-024 anchor; 1:1 direct via the explicit two-participant list; private via the derived set PLUS the explicit per-record sharing grant (task 002 mechanism).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the reconcile step: desired = derived set (mapped to `communicationUserId` via the identity map from task 010); current = ACS thread participants; enforce `desired ⊇ ACS` invariant — Add (desired \ current), Remove (current \ desired) via task 011's server-side ACS ops. Never add beyond desired.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire the reconcile job on the existing Service Bus job contract: idempotent (re-running on a consistent thread is a no-op), retry with backoff, DLQ on repeated failure. Trigger event-driven (Dataverse record-access change | privacy switch | participant edit) AND via a periodic sweep.</step>
    <step order="6">Write an audit entry per membership change (participant added/removed, thread, reason/trigger, timestamp, actor).</step>
    <step order="7">Make reconcile best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02): a failure logs + retries + DLQs; it does NOT fail send/capture; the sweep repairs drift.</step>
    <step order="8">Register the derivation service + reconcile job via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if any part is feature-gated).</step>
    <step order="9">Write tests: open-thread membership matches the ADR-034 derived set; a Dataverse access change reconciles ACS membership within the sweep window; ACS membership NEVER exceeds the derived set (over-exposure guard); an audit entry is recorded per change; a reconcile failure does not fail the persist path (NFR-02).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` then `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-041-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: projection invariant — ACS ⊆ Dataverse-derived; NFR-02 non-fatal; ADR-034 reuse; §11 justification); `adr-check` against `spec.md`. Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="9.6">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (041 ✅) + reset `current-task.md`; record decisions (derivation mapping, sweep cadence, audit shape, trigger events).</step>
  </steps>

